["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/specType", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A specification type defines the nature of a specification.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/AI/limitation", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A free-form text that captures a limitation of the AI package\n(or of the AI models present in the AI package).\n\nNote that this is not guaranteed to be exhaustive.\n\nFor instance, a limitation can be that the AI package is having poor accuracy\nfor a certain demography.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security/CvssSeverityType/none", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/ResponsibilityType/custody", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "International Standard Content Code (ISCC) <https://iscc.io/> is a content-derived identifier standardized by ISO 24138 <https://www.iso.org/standard/77899.html> for identifying digital assets. ISCC can be used in conjunction with other schemes, such as DOI, ISAN, ISBN, ISRC, ISSN and ISWC. A standard ISCC-CODE is build from multiple ISCC-UNITs. Each unit serve a different purpose. An ISCC-CODE typically look like ISCC:KACT4EBWK27737D2AYCJRAL5Z36G76RFRMO4554RU26HZ4ORJGIVHDI.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Ndeb9000392da4a5d90dcc0017dd6df20", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isrc", "globalId", "", ""]
