["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/isoAutomationLevel", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "The level of automation describes a spectrum of system capability, defining\nthe degree of control and decision-making authority a system possesses\nrelative to an external control.\n\nThis classification helps to define the roles and responsibilities of both the\nhuman operator and the automated system. It is a critical component for risk\nassessment, regulatory compliance, and user interface design.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose/firmware", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The Element provides low level control over a device's hardware.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Ne1fda7a8723548b6b5141b17b45c3ed8", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:N76011861651a413c9a956a2dc502b9a1", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/SpecificationType/specification", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "A specification is a detailed document (or set of documents) that describes the requirements, design, behavior, or other characteristics of a system, component, or process so that all stakeholders have a clear, unambiguous reference.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
